## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement a simple, reliable streaming ingest with validation, a practical approach to schema evolution, and basic operations like dead-lettering, archiving, rollback, and monitoring at beginner level.

## Key Concepts

- Pub/Sub as a source and dead-lettering for bad messages
- Dataflow (Beam) for parsing/validation
- BigQuery core schema + extras JSON field for evolution
- Idempotent writes using insertId or MERGE
- Rollback strategies using Pub/Sub replay or GCS archive
- Basic monitoring and alerts for data quality

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-beam style pseudocode
// Read from Pub/Sub, parse JSON, validate required fields, emit rows to BigQuery
class ParseAndValidateDoFn extends DoFn {
  processElement(ctx) {
    const msg = JSON.parse(ctx.element);
    if (!msg.timestamp || !msg.user_id || !msg.endpoint) return;
    const row = {core_field1: msg.timestamp, core_field2: msg.user_id, core_field3: msg.endpoint, extras: JSON.stringify(msg.extras || {})};
    yield row;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test schema-evolution choices and measure their impact on query performance?
- What would you monitor to detect data quality regressions in this pipeline?

## Why This Is Asked
This angle explores multi-tenant isolation, masking, and rollback in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts
- Dataflow (Beam) streaming pipelines
- Pub/Sub for ingestion
- Per-tenant BigQuery datasets
- Data Loss Prevention masking in ingest
- Idempotent writes with MERGE
- Dead-letter queues and raw data archiving
- 24h rollback via replay from Cloud Storage
- Observability through Dataflow metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Dataflow masking sketch (pseudo)
class MaskPII {
  process(element) {
    if (element.email) element.email = '*****@*****.com';
    if (element.phone) element.phone = '**********';
    return element;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test data quality across tenants? 
- How would you enforce per-tenant quotas in BigQuery and Dataflow?

## Why This Is Asked
Understanding end-to-end streaming ingestion, privacy handling, and basic rollback in GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub streaming
- Dataflow DoFn masking
- BigQuery per-tenant datasets
- Data Catalog data contracts and lineage
- Quarantine path and 24h rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow DoFn: mask PII before write
class MaskPIIFn {
  process(element) {
    // element is a JSON object
    if (element.email) element.email = maskEmail(element.email);
    if (element.phone) element.phone = maskPhone(element.phone);
    return element;
  }
}
```

